    "evidence_text": "Nansen Ski Jump\n\n Built in 1936, it was the largest ski jump of its time.\n\nPictou County Wellness Centre\n\nThe Pictou County Wellness Centre is a, multi-purpose sporting facility located in New Glasgow, Nova Scotia.\n\n The facility opened on December 6, 2012.\n\n The opening day featured a MHL game between the Pictou County Crushers and the Bridgewater Lumberjacks.\n\nClarence Aquatic Centre\n\nLancaster, New Hampshire\n\nLancaster is a town in Coos County, New Hampshire, United States, on the Connecticut River.\n\n It is the county seat of Coos County and gateway to the Great North Woods Region.\n\n Part of the White Mountain National Forest is in the eastern portion.\n\nRath Eastlink Community Centre\n\nCoos Bay, Oregon\n\nSir Bruce Small Park\n\n It has hosted many high profile Australian baseball events such as the Masters Games and University Games.\n\nGarcelon Civic Centre\n\nThe Garcelon Civic Centre is a, multi-purpose sporting facility located in St. Stephen, New Brunswick.\n\nState Netball and Hockey Centre\n\n The facility is located in Royal Park, Parkville next to the Melbourne Zoo.\n\n and consists of two outdoor hockey fields, four outdoor and five indoor netball courts.\n\nMilan, New Hampshire\nMilan ( ) is a town in Coos County, New Hampshire, United States.\n The population was 1,337 at the 2010 census.\n It is part of the Berlin, NH\u2013VT Micropolitan Statistical Area.",
